      "description": "Watch Paksi SE vs Panathinaikos highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 24, 2026. The UEFA Europa Conference League clash between Paksi SE and Panathinaikos on July 24, 2026, provided a fascinating display of European football dynamics. Both sides entered the arena with high expectations, looking to secure a foothold in a competition known for its unpredictable drama. First Half Misfortune The opening period was largely a tactical stalemate, with clear-cut chances at a premium as both defenses remained organized. However, the deadlock was broken in a cruel fashion for the home side in the 41st minute. Gabor Vas accidentally diverted the ball into his own net, gifting Panathinaikos a 1-0 lead just before the halftime whistle blew, leaving the home fans in stunned silence. Valencia Strikes as Tensions Rise Returning for the second half, the intensity ramped up significantly. Panathinaikos showed their steel, though it came at a cost with yellow cards for Triantafyllos Tsapras and Adam Gnezda Cerin . Their persistence paid off in the 56th minute when Santino Andino Valencia doubled the lead with a composed finish. Facing a two-goal deficit, Paksi SE manager opted for a triple substitution, bringing on the likes of Daniel Bode to spark a revival. Bode Ignites a Late Charge The tactical gamble paid dividends in the 71st minute. Kevin Horvath , another second-half introduction, found Daniel Bode , who made no mistake in slotting the ball home to make it 1-2. The final twenty minutes were a frantic affair as the Hungarian side pushed for an equalizer. Despite a late booking for Pavlos Pantelidis and five minutes of stoppage time, the Greek visitors held firm to see out a tense victory."
